## Scams to recognise on sight

| The setup | The red flag | What to do |
|-----------|-------------|------------|
| "Accept this cashback on UPI" | PIN needed to receive = sending, not receiving | Reject. Block. Report. |
| Customer care calls about a failed transaction | Asks for OTP or PIN | Hang up. Call your bank directly using the number on their website. |
| "Send ₹1 to verify your account" | Legitimate services never ask you to send money first | Refuse. Always. |
| Someone sends you ₹1 and asks you to "return ₹1000 by mistake" | Classic trick — the ₹1 never actually arrives | Don't send anything. Block. |
| QR code sent to "receive" payment | Scanning a QR to receive money doesn't require a PIN | Question the logic. Then reject. |

